        "kind": "ai-tool-descriptor",
        "id": "tool:share-anything",
        "label": "Share anything",
        "status": "active",
        "job": "Share anything of mine read-only, from one record or one piece of text to a whole list or any mix of records, with a person, an AI or anyone holding a link, or let named people and AIs run some of my tools at my door with no copy on their computer; show who has access; and stop it",
        "description": "op share (the default job): give grant (sharing: plus the thing's label; read-data/share-label.mjs grantOf makes it, and the answer of any earlier call names it), thing (one of { type, id }, { list } for a list and all its rows, { text, title? } for a piece of text, or { items: [{ type, id? | prefix? }], title } for any mix) and who: with (a list of names of people or AIs, each given a key of its own) and/or link: true (one key anyone can hold). Optional until (a future ISO time the view share ends) and origin (https:// address that opens a link: url is then origin/share/<key>). A view share only lets people view (can: [\"view\"], the default). It keeps the share as one record of yours and answers each key once: the key itself is not kept anywhere, only a digest of it, so lose it and share again after stopping. A person or AI presents the key at your door, and the engine reads what was shared there; a person opens the url in a browser. op stop: give grant, and principal to stop one person (principal \"link\" stops the link), or leave principal out to stop everyone. op access: give grant; answers who can open it now (people with when added, the link, until when, whether it is open, stopped or ended), never a key. To let people run tools instead: can [\"run\"] with grant (sharing: plus a name you choose), tools (Workshop tool ids, tool:...), with (names of people or AIs: letters, digits, _ or -), an optional end rule you choose (until, a future ISO time; unused_days, whole days with no use; or both, the earlier ends it; by default it has no end and stands until you stop it), identity (none, the default: your side learns nothing of who runs; self: the tool's input gets their name) and journal (input, the default, or none). Each person gets a key of their own, answered once; they or any MCP client of theirs present it at your door and can list and run only those tools there. op stop and op access take can [\"run\"] and grant the same way; stopping a person or everyone ends their next call. op end with can [\"run\"] and grant sets the end rule again (until and/or unused_days, or neither for no end), and the people keep their keys. The rule is kept beside the share and the engine never reads it: tool:end-shares-whose-condition-failed, given the run shares the store lists, returns the withdrawal of each whose rule says it has ended.",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": [
            "grant"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "op": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "share",
                "stop",
                "access",
                "end"
              ],
              "default": "share"
            },
            "grant": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 9,
              "maxLength": 400,
              "description": "Where the share is kept: sharing: plus the thing's label"
            },
            "thing": {
              "type": "object",
              "description": "What is shared: one of { type, id } (one record), { list } (a list and all its rows), { text, title? } (a piece of text) or { items: [{ type, id? | prefix? }], title } (any mix; an item with neither id nor prefix is every record of that type). The share's label is read-data/share-label.mjs labelOf.",
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "type": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "id": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "list": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "A list's id, with or without list:"
                },
                "text": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "title": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "items": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "minItems": 1,
                  "maxItems": 64,
                  "items": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "required": [
                      "type"
                    ],
                    "properties": {
                      "type": {
                        "type": "string"
                      },
                      "id": {
                        "type": "string"
                      },
                      "prefix": {
                        "type": "string"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "with": {
              "type": "array",
              "maxItems": 64,
              "items": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "principal"
                    ],
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "properties": {
                      "principal": {
                        "type": "string"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "description": "Who to share with: names of people or AIs"
            },
            "link": {
              "type": "boolean",
              "description": "Also make one link anyone holding it can open"
            },
            "can": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "view",
                  "run"
                ]
              },
              "description": "What people can do: [\"view\"] (the default) or [\"run\"] the tools named in tools"
            },
            "until": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "When the share ends: a future ISO time. A view share is read against it by the engine of the share. A run share keeps it in its end rule (null with op end clears it); by default a run share has no end."
            },
            "unused_days": {
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ],
              "minimum": 1,
              "description": "With can [\"run\"]: the share ends after this many days with no use, each use starting the days again (null with op end clears it). No default: left out, the share has no such end."
            },
            "origin": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "https:// address a link opens on"
            },
            "title": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "What the share is called; the thing's own name when left out"
            },
            "principal": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "stop: the one person or AI to stop (link for the link); everyone when left out"
            },
            "now": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "The time to decide at (ISO); now when left out"
            },
            "tools": {
              "type": "array",
              "minItems": 1,
              "maxItems": 64,
              "items": {
                "type": "string",
                "minLength": 1
              },
              "description": "With can [\"run\"]: the Workshop tool ids the people may run at your door"
            },
            "identity": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "none",
                "self"
              ],
              "description": "With can [\"run\"]: none (default) tells your side nothing of who runs; self puts their name in the tool's input"
            },
            "journal": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "input",
                "none"
              ],
              "description": "With can [\"run\"]: input (default) keeps a digest of what they sent in your journal; none keeps none"
            },
            "stored": {
              "type": "object",
              "description": "What the run reads from the person's own store and gives here, as the store holds it (null or left out when it holds nothing): kept, the value at grant (a share record; for a run share the grant as listed: {grant, people, ends, last_used}); list, the list definition list:<id> when thing is a list (its row_type and label). The tool reads no store: a caller that does, reads these and writes back what the answer's writes say, each only while the store still holds its expect."
            }
          }
        },
        "output_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "op",
            "label",
